# .auditignore — npm audit exception list
# =============================================================================
#
# PURPOSE
# -------
# This file lists vulnerability IDs that are intentionally accepted and should
# NOT cause the security-scan CI job to fail.
#
# WHEN TO ADD AN ENTRY
# --------------------
# Only add an exception when ALL of the following are true:
#   1. You have reviewed the advisory and confirmed the vulnerability does NOT
#      affect this project in its current usage context.
#   2. No patched version of the package is available yet, OR upgrading would
#      require a disproportionate effort relative to the actual risk.
#   3. You have documented the rationale and set a realistic expiry date.
#
# EVERY EXCEPTION MUST HAVE A RATIONALE. Entries without a reason will be
# removed during the next security review.
#
# FORMAT
# ------
# Each active (non-commented) exception occupies a single line:
#
#   VULN-ID | package-name | reason | expires: YYYY-MM-DD
#
# Fields:
#   VULN-ID      — The vulnerability identifier (npm advisory source ID,
#                  GitHub Advisory ID such as GHSA-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx, or CVE).
#   package-name — The exact npm package name affected.
#   reason       — A short human-readable justification (no pipes "|" allowed).
#   expires      — ISO-8601 date after which this exception MUST be re-evaluated.
#                  The CI job will NOT enforce expiry automatically; the security
#                  team is responsible for reviewing and removing stale entries.
#
# EXAMPLE ENTRIES (all commented out — do not uncomment without review)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1234567 | lodash | Prototype-pollution in _.merge; we only call _.pick on
#          trusted server-side data. No user input reaches the affected path.
#          expires: 2026-12-31

# GHSA-abc1-def2-ghi3 | axios | ReDoS in URL parsing; our usage passes only
#                       hard-coded base URLs — no user-controlled input is
#                       present in the URL string. Re-evaluate after axios@2.x
#                       release. expires: 2027-03-31

# CVE-2025-99999 | semver | ReDOS in semver range parsing; only invoked during
#                  build-time version resolution, never on untrusted input.
#                  expires: 2026-06-30

# =============================================================================
# Active exceptions below this line
# (none at this time — add entries as VULN-ID | package | reason | expires: DATE)
# =============================================================================
